# LAND-DISPLACE: landscape displacement (UE 5.4+ landscape displacement) - the layers' height maps move the ground's
# vertices (diced near cells, LandscapeDisplacement.glslh); M_FieldBarn_Landscape: Magnitude 20 cm, Center 0.5,
# Fade 8..15 m. Dice rings around the camera (16/8/4/2/1 sub-cells a side, edge = min of the two cells). Off = Scalability ViewDistance Low (DisplacementDicingRate 0), as mesh displacement (DISPLACE).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance Cinematic"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 25
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 110
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 1700,640,-2050
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.1,-0.35,-1
Тогда 1_on ground 2-15 m ahead shows raised bumps: uneven silhouette at the ridge line, bumps cast short shadows on the ground beside them, grass/props stand on the surface (no floating)
Когда run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance Low"
Тогда 2_off same view, flat ground (dicing rate 0), the difference to 1_on obvious
Когда run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance Cinematic"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 1650,720,-1200
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.04,-0.12,-1
Тогда 3_far low along the path to the barn: relief near, fading out by 15 m with no seam, crack or step at the fade or between dice rings/tiles
